00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.515
So I'm in DC.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's a very, we've
been very busy.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.454
I just got back from tour.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:88% position:13%
You're on the short list
of people I would've

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.891
been willing to have
here at the house.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.293 align:start size:84% position:16%
But let's dive
right into the book,

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
because first off I've
got it in my hand.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.497
This is a dense, powerful book,

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.300
full of a whole bunch of the
ideas that you've been talking

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.769 align:start size:84% position:16%
about for really
decades at this point.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.972
But I wanna read just
the first paragraph off

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.507
the back flap here,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think you say
something very interesting

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.445
that I think is the thing that
sort of connects both of us.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:56.182
You say Conservatism, as
we know, it has failed.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:59.085
While Liberalism was
eroding the foundations

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:02.322
of our culture, the family,
the nation and religion,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.426
Conservatives adopted
the very principles

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.628
that ensured their defeat.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:12.432
Routinely confused with
Classical Liberalism,

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.768
Conservatism found
itself defenseless

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:19.506
before a ferocious
and relentless foe.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:23.877 align:start size:97% position:3%
All right, now, you know,
I'm Mister Classical Liberal.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.546 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think I helped
bring that phrase back

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.947
into the American lexicon.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
But you also know that
I have found faults

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.920
within the Liberal lens.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.288
We've discussed them before,

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we've discussed
them at NatCon actually,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.325
just a couple months
back here in Florida.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:43.730
So what brings you, well, first,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:84% position:16%
let me let you
define Conservatism,

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how it's different
than Classical Liberalism,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.702
and then we'll go from there.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:58.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Conservatism's
an Anglo-American
political tradition.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:97% position:3%
It goes back many centuries
long before Burke,

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.583
And it's a tradition that

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:08.521
puts the idea of transmission

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:12.292
and stability of the
nation at the center.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:15.028
So a Conservative is always
going to be asking questions

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.831
like, "Have we upheld

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.235 align:start size:84% position:16%
the main principles,
traditions that

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:25.438
are holding our
people together?"

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.706
That can't go on forever.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.341
There's always deterioration.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's always
things that change.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:32.212
And then a Conservative
is gonna be looking back

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:37.083
when something starts to
fall apart and saying,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.319
"What can we restore?"

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.755
What can we go back
to that used to work

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we really need and
are sorry that we've lost?

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.727 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So I think a lot of
people are hearing that,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.796
and that's pretty
clean and clear

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:52.365
that there were some hard
fought things of the past

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.633
that we should remember,

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:57.270
and perhaps bring back
into our daily lives.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:01.241
Does Classical Liberalism not
grab a hold of all of that?

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.042
What's the problem there?

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.913 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, Classical
Liberalism is something that

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.183
is based on, like,
if you take a look at

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:13.786
the big thinkers of
the Enlightenment,

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:88% position:13%
the rationalist thinkers
of the Enlightenment,

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.925
who originally designed this.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.063
Liberalism, it's a
set of principles

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:28.901
that begin with every human
being is by nature free,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.137
perfectly free and
perfectly equal.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.773
And the purpose of government

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
is to give the
individual, to protect

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.546 align:start size:84% position:16%
the rights and
equalities that belong

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.448
to the individual by nature.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:46.519
So the entire set of ideas that,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:51.491 align:start size:97% position:3%
that are at the basis of
Liberalism they're basically,

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.259
you know, lots of
people said this,

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:56.095
they're basically, they are
a philosophy of freedom.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:05:01.034
They're a way of thinking about,

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.136
how do we work it so that people

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.372
are maximally free
and unconstrained?"

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.908 align:start size:81% position:19%
And the problem
is, and this is...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.112
This is something very
deep and very serious

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:17.517
that I really think we need
to be talking about much more

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:22.522
is that human beings do not
only need freedom by nature.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.692
And if you think human
beings only need freedom,

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
then I think you've
got a mistaken

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.462
and misleading philosophy.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:32.498
Human beings need
to be constrained.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
They need to have
guardrails and guidelines.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
They need to be encouraged
to do the things

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.143
that are needed in order
to keep their society,

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:48.014 align:start size:97% position:3%
their people, their
families, to keep it going.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:53.019 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it used to be that I
would say after World War II,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was a very, very
strong impulse in America,

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.323
and across Europe to say,

00:05:57.323 --> 00:06:00.593
"Look, Liberalism is
all, it's all we need.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:02.895
Private people will
make the decisions

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
about where the
guardrails should be,

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.600
what the constraints should be.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.839 align:start size:88% position:13%
Maybe that made sense
to a lot of people then.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:16.376 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think at this point, we've
reached the point where,

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:19.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, we're looking across
America and across Europe.

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:22.715
I mean, I think it's scary.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:26.252
I think you can see
the chaos coming.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:32.125 align:start size:97% position:3%
The assumption of Liberalism
is let people argue

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.628
and be freely speak
and freely argue,

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.930
and they'll come to
the right decisions.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.600
But I would say since 2020,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.369
we're looking at an
America, that is,

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:46.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
is just, it's
tottering on having...

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:50.643 align:start size:97% position:3%
The woke neo-Marxist
ideology become kind of like

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:55.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
the public ideology
of the state.

00:06:55.148 --> 00:07:00.153
And if you look sort of on the
edges of the political right,

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.156
like beyond Conservatism,

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:07.393
there's fast growing thinkers.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:11.697 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean that a lot of
the kids are reading who

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.266
are arguing for dictatorship.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:16.302
They're just saying,
"Look, the whole idea

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:18.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the American
Constitution has failed,"

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:22.241
and they're looking
to dictatorship.

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:26.279 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I think it's becoming
really, really clear

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:29.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
that if we don't start
talking about conservation,

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:31.584
and transmission,
and restoration,

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:33.786
like a lot and focusing on it,

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:37.924
I think America is in danger
and I think it's in danger

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:40.793 align:start size:97% position:3%
of taking like the
Democratic countries with it.

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:42.395 align:start size:97% position:3%
- All right, so you're
hitting on a lot of the stuff

00:07:42.395 --> 00:07:44.063
that obviously I focus on.

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:48.000 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I'm proud to say that
at the end of my first book,

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.204
"Don't Burn This Book," I
made an argument related

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.739
to God and belief
connecting some

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:56.943 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the classic Liberal
beliefs to that,

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I saw what
you're now talking about.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.981
I sort of saw it on the horizon

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.950
that we could get to this point.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:07.253 align:start position:0%
So first, do you think, is
that a flow flaw in Liberalism,

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:10.423
or is that a flaw
in human nature,

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.992
or is there even a
distinction there?

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:15.995 align:start size:84% position:16%
In that from say World
War II 'til about,

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.231
I don't know, maybe
five, 10 years ago,

00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:21.067
the Liberal order
sort of worked.

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:22.468
Or I don't wanna put
words in your mouth.

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.170
In my estimation,
it sort of worked,

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:28.074
and then suddenly this
woke parasite got inside.

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:30.276 align:start size:84% position:16%
But would you say
that it roughly worked

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:31.878
for a certain amount of decades?

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.581
- Well, I think it's
been running down.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:40.653
Look, I think, I think
2020 was a shocking,

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:44.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a shocking year in
terms of just institutions

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.626
all the way from
the New York Times

00:08:46.626 --> 00:08:49.462
to Princeton University,
just being taken over.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:50.730
I think it was a shocking year.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:54.000
And I don't wanna say that,

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
there was obvious
that was gonna happen.

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:59.639 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I think as I write
in this new book,

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:04.577
I think the deterioration
has been really clear,

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:06.546
you know, almost a straight line

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:10.616
since the 1960s, even the 1940s.

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:13.352
But 1960s is when,

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:19.091 align:start size:84% position:16%
is when there's
this final decision

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:22.762 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the United States
is gonna ban God,

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:25.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
religious tradition,
prayer, Bible,

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:28.467 align:start size:84% position:16%
just ban it outright
more or less

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:31.470
from schools across the country.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:36.342
And the theory behind it
was people said, "Look,

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:40.680
our country, we live
in a Christian country.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.215 align:start size:88% position:13%
Overwhelming majority
of people are Christian.

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:45.718
We can be tolerant and
decent to other people,

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:48.454
but basically it's
a Christian country.

00:09:48.454 --> 00:09:51.023
So we don't have to have
this stuff in the schools.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.994
I think pretty much since then

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:58.798 line:0%
the assumption that you could

00:09:58.798 --> 00:10:02.101 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
just take God and scripture
out of the schools,

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:05.304
and it would continue to live,

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:07.440
on Sundays and in
people's homes.

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.142
I think that turned
out not to be true.

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:14.246
And what happened is first
in the name of equality,

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:17.917
and freedom from religion,

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:20.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
and everybody being
treated equal,

00:10:20.419 --> 00:10:22.021
all religion was removed

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:24.256
from the schools,
God and scripture.

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:27.760
And after that then,

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:32.164 align:start size:84% position:16%
the idea of an
independent nation,

00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:34.800
or of the family ended up kind

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.436
of being eliminated
from the schools.

00:10:37.436 --> 00:10:41.874
And by this point, even
the idea of man and woman

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:46.078 align:start size:84% position:16%
being the basis of the
traditional family,

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:48.581
that's also now in
the name of equality,

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:52.385
and freedom from religion,
that's also been eliminated.

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:55.655
As I understand it,

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:01.060
it's been a one
way ratchet where

00:11:01.994 --> 00:11:04.263
every 10 years, something else

00:11:04.263 --> 00:11:08.034 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we will sorely
miss has been removed.

00:11:12.638 --> 00:11:16.008
People just don't don't
know what to do with it.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:19.879
I mean, I really think
an awful lot of people

00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:23.149
in America and other
countries are saying,

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:25.351
"Look, this is just the
fall of the Roman Empire.

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:26.686
This is just the end."

00:11:28.721 --> 00:11:32.391 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can't remove every
single, basic building block

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:35.828 align:start size:88% position:13%
of the way we built
society, throw it away,

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:38.130 align:start size:84% position:16%
open it to question,
and then think

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.733
that there's gonna be
anything but chaos.

00:11:42.535 --> 00:11:45.104
That's pretty much what
looks like it's coming.

00:11:45.104 --> 00:11:47.740
- Right. Chaos seems
to be at our doorstep.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:50.142 align:start size:84% position:16%
So do you think
secular institutions

00:11:50.142 --> 00:11:53.079
simply cannot work at all?

00:11:53.079 --> 00:11:55.147
I mean, basically what
you're saying is there,

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:58.884 align:start position:0%
well, I guess everything is
gonna degrade over time, right?

00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:01.420
- Everything degrades over time.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:05.224
The question is, are
you helping it degrade,

00:12:05.224 --> 00:12:07.927
or are you working
for a restoration?

00:12:07.927 --> 00:12:10.296
Where you can see that
a mistake has been made,

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:12.364
so you can act to
try to stop it.

00:12:12.364 --> 00:12:16.102 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, Dave, I'm a religious
person, in the end.

00:12:17.436 --> 00:12:19.505
In the end, I think,

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:22.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have to do what looks
right to us the best we can.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:25.144
In the end, we're really
bad at seeing the future.

00:12:25.144 --> 00:12:27.546
And what's gonna
happen is gonna,

00:12:27.546 --> 00:12:29.415
God decides in the end,

00:12:29.415 --> 00:12:31.283
what's gonna come of
all of our efforts.

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:36.255
But we have an obligation
to try to restore things,

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:41.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
to try to restore respect
for the American Constitution

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:43.696 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the Anglo-American
legal tradition.

00:12:43.696 --> 00:12:45.731
We have to try to
restore respect

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:48.033
for the traditional family,

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.803
and for the Bible and for God.

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:55.908
That's up to us to try to
do, and maybe it'll work.

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:57.877
- So I think a certain amount
of people are watching this,

00:12:57.877 --> 00:13:01.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what they may not
know is on the other side

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.983 align:start size:84% position:16%
of that very fine head
of hair, my friend

00:13:03.983 --> 00:13:05.518
is a yamaka back there.

00:13:05.518 --> 00:13:08.654
You are an Orthodox Jew,
you live in Jerusalem.

00:13:08.654 --> 00:13:12.291 align:start size:97% position:3%
And yet, here you are
talking about Anglo beliefs,

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:15.694 align:start size:84% position:16%
a Christian America,
things like that.

00:13:15.694 --> 00:13:17.596
I was on a panel
with you at NatCon,

00:13:17.596 --> 00:13:20.599
where we were trying
to sort of work out,

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:22.768
it was the two of us
and Sohrab Ahmari,

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:24.036
who I've had on the show,

00:13:24.036 --> 00:13:25.504
and Douglas Murray, who
I've had on many times.

00:13:25.504 --> 00:13:28.607
Trying to sort of
whittle out where,

00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:30.276
if you were to go back to some

00:13:30.276 --> 00:13:31.744
of what you're calling for,

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:34.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a national
conservative country,

00:13:34.613 --> 00:13:36.148
what happens to the minorities?

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:38.284
What happens to the
religious minorities?

00:13:38.284 --> 00:13:41.921
What happens to people that
don't necessary prescribe

00:13:41.921 --> 00:13:44.924
to all of the sort
of religious set

00:13:44.924 --> 00:13:46.959 align:start size:84% position:16%
of views that you're
including here?

00:13:46.959 --> 00:13:48.294
So what do we do with that?

00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:54.033
- The book deals with
two different fronts.

00:13:54.033 --> 00:13:56.202
One, is the question
you're asking me now,

00:13:56.202 --> 00:14:01.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is about the public
life of the country.

00:14:02.308 --> 00:14:04.243
And the other part
of the book deals

00:14:04.243 --> 00:14:06.679
with our private lives.

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:09.048
Because people tend to think
these things are unrelated.

00:14:09.048 --> 00:14:11.183
I think they're
deeply connected.

00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:14.553
And so the book is really
an argument for people

00:14:15.788 --> 00:14:18.190
to drop the idea that
you can just argue

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.925
for Conservative policy.

00:14:19.925 --> 00:14:23.195 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think that you have to also
lead a Conservative life.

00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:26.665
You have to come back
to a Conservative life,

00:14:26.665 --> 00:14:28.400
and be a Conservative person.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:30.202
So those two things.

00:14:30.202 --> 00:14:33.873
Now, when I talk about
Conservative democracy,

00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:36.008
I'm talking about a democracy.

00:14:36.008 --> 00:14:40.779
I'm talking about the kind of
democracy that America was.

00:14:42.414 --> 00:14:44.450
Sure, there's some
things from the past

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.051
that we should never go back to.

00:14:47.219 --> 00:14:50.522
Slavery and persecution
of Blacks in America,

00:14:50.522 --> 00:14:53.459
just as the most
obvious example.

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.094 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't know any
Conservative that wants

00:14:55.094 --> 00:14:56.362
to go back to that.

00:14:56.362 --> 00:14:58.530
In fact, in my book
I make the argument

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:02.368
that that was a deviation from
the Anglo-American tradition

00:15:02.368 --> 00:15:04.470
which is for a very long time

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:07.473 align:start size:97% position:3%
was anti-slavery before
there were slaves in America.

00:15:09.041 --> 00:15:12.244
But since I'm arguing for
democracy I'm still talking

00:15:12.244 --> 00:15:15.881 align:start size:84% position:16%
about the political
framework where

00:15:15.881 --> 00:15:17.850
this should not be
imposed on anybody.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.453
We're talking about those states

00:15:21.453 --> 00:15:24.189
that still have a
Christian majority.

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or let's say maybe
there's Orthodox Jews who

00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:31.196
would support this kind
of thing, or others.

00:15:31.196 --> 00:15:35.367
So those states, those
regions, those places

00:15:35.367 --> 00:15:37.436
where there's still a desire

00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:41.640
to lead a Democratic life.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:46.645
But where the public
philosophy, let's say,

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:49.982
is not neo-Marxism.

00:15:49.982 --> 00:15:51.483
The public philosophy is going

00:15:51.483 --> 00:15:53.819
to be based on a
Biblical vision,

00:15:53.819 --> 00:15:57.656 align:start size:81% position:19%
on a Christian
and Jewish vision.

00:15:57.656 --> 00:16:02.594
And my assumption is that
anybody who actually wants

00:16:03.762 --> 00:16:05.197
to do this, I'm not
just assuming it,

00:16:05.197 --> 00:16:06.398
I mean this is what I...

00:16:08.267 --> 00:16:10.669 align:start size:88% position:13%
I talk to Catholics, and
Protestants and Jews.

00:16:11.837 --> 00:16:13.605
I talk to them and try
to understand people

00:16:13.605 --> 00:16:16.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
from all over the
country, what's possible?

00:16:16.675 --> 00:16:20.913
And I believe that there is a,

00:16:20.913 --> 00:16:23.749
the people looking
at sort of the cliff

00:16:25.818 --> 00:16:28.354
that America's just
hurtling towards

00:16:28.354 --> 00:16:31.023
this cliff and about to go over.

00:16:31.023 --> 00:16:34.226 align:start position:0%
I think an awful lot of
people, Protestants, Catholics,

00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:38.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
and Jews, and others
would be willing

00:16:38.364 --> 00:16:41.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
to negotiate some
kind of a return of,

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:48.640
let's say the basic,
Christian moral vision.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.743
To be like the public
background against

00:16:50.743 --> 00:16:55.447 align:start size:88% position:13%
which things are
operate, in some places.

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:57.216
I mean, in some
states in the US.

00:16:57.216 --> 00:17:00.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think the
Conservative way to do this

00:17:00.386 --> 00:17:05.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
is not to have the
Supreme Court dictate this

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.792
to people who don't want it.

00:17:06.792 --> 00:17:09.528
The Conservative way to do
it is to experiment with it

00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:11.397
in those places that want it,

00:17:11.397 --> 00:17:14.500
so that we can see what
does this add up to?

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:18.070 align:start size:88% position:13%
Instead of like saying,
"Well, Christians

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
were always terrible
throughout their history."

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:21.540
Let's see what the Christian,

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.808 align:start size:84% position:16%
which I don't
believe, by the way.

00:17:22.808 --> 00:17:26.311
But instead of that
argument in the air,

00:17:26.311 --> 00:17:28.881 align:start size:84% position:16%
we should do an
experiment, let's see.

00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:33.886
Let's see what does a, what
do the Christians in America,

00:17:35.821 --> 00:17:38.490
when they get to be
the public culture

00:17:39.658 --> 00:17:41.627
in a few states,
what do they do?

00:17:42.995 --> 00:17:46.131 align:start size:97% position:3%
If it's better, and I'm
guessing it's gonna be better,

00:17:46.131 --> 00:17:48.400
if it's better, so people
will want to move there,

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.935
and other states will adopt it.

00:17:49.935 --> 00:17:53.939
And if it's as terrible as
everybody's always saying

00:17:56.675 --> 00:17:58.744 align:start size:88% position:13%
to let the Christians
where they're a majority

00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:02.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
to let them have the
public, if it's so awful.

00:18:02.081 --> 00:18:03.749
So we'll see that it's
awful, and we'll say,

00:18:03.749 --> 00:18:05.451 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Okay, we tried that,
that didn't work.

00:18:05.451 --> 00:18:06.852
Let's do something else."

00:18:06.852 --> 00:18:08.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So do you see something
like what's going

00:18:08.921 --> 00:18:12.658
on here in Florida, where
I think we're defending

00:18:12.658 --> 00:18:15.027 align:start size:84% position:16%
almost everything
you're talking about,

00:18:15.027 --> 00:18:17.262 align:start size:84% position:16%
but not from the
religious perspective.

00:18:17.262 --> 00:18:19.765
In that the governor is
up there talking about

00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:21.366 align:start size:84% position:16%
this stuff from a
religious perspective.

00:18:21.366 --> 00:18:23.068
However, he's doing
a lot of the work

00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:24.236
that I think you're calling for.

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:25.504
- Yup.

00:18:25.504 --> 00:18:26.939
- He is acknowledging
differences biological

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:28.607 align:start size:84% position:16%
between boys and
girls, and getting rid

00:18:28.607 --> 00:18:31.543 align:start size:88% position:13%
of critical race theory
out of the schools.

00:18:31.543 --> 00:18:32.978
And he's fighting
against against

00:18:32.978 --> 00:18:34.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
a constantly overreaching
federal government,

00:18:34.913 --> 00:18:36.215
all those things.

00:18:36.215 --> 00:18:38.684
I think I sense that
you still think that

00:18:38.684 --> 00:18:41.186 align:start size:84% position:16%
that may not be enough
for the experiment

00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:42.454
as you wanted, is that right?

00:18:42.454 --> 00:18:44.890
- No, I don't think it's enough.

00:18:46.825 --> 00:18:51.196
The basic problem is
that for many years

00:18:53.532 --> 00:18:56.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
most Liberal scholars
and professors who talked

00:18:56.301 --> 00:18:59.037
about this kind of
things, theorists,

00:18:59.037 --> 00:19:02.040 align:start size:97% position:3%
they talked about Liberalism
as a neutral state.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:04.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like a state that
wouldn't actually have

00:19:04.843 --> 00:19:06.378
any kind of moral vision.

00:19:06.378 --> 00:19:07.646
It would just be neutral

00:19:07.646 --> 00:19:09.348
and let everybody
do what they want.

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:14.386
This book argues, I mean, I'm
certainly not the only one,

00:19:14.386 --> 00:19:18.957
but I'm arguing, there is no
such thing as a neutral state.

00:19:18.957 --> 00:19:22.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can try it,
but it continues to

00:19:22.294 --> 00:19:26.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
be mostly Christian
values up until the moment

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:27.866
that it just falls apart,

00:19:27.866 --> 00:19:31.537
and you suddenly realize
that it's anti-Christian.

00:19:31.537 --> 00:19:33.939
And I think that's
what's happening,

00:19:33.939 --> 00:19:35.674 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's what's
happening in America,

00:19:35.674 --> 00:19:38.010
and in Britain, and
in other places, too.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:42.214
Is that there is a
public philosophy.

00:19:42.214 --> 00:19:43.782
But that public philosophy

00:19:43.782 --> 00:19:46.151 align:start size:81% position:19%
is progressive,
woke, neo-Marxism.

00:19:48.453 --> 00:19:51.423
I know that there are a
lot of good Liberals who,

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:55.527
they want to hold
on to the idea of,

00:19:55.527 --> 00:19:58.997 align:start size:88% position:13%
well, let's just go
back to a neutral state.

00:19:58.997 --> 00:20:03.735 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think they just
don't understand that

00:20:03.735 --> 00:20:06.772 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's collapsed, and it
hasn't collapsed by accident.

00:20:07.873 --> 00:20:09.741 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's collapsed
because of the fact

00:20:09.741 --> 00:20:12.544
that when you're saying,
"No, the state is neutral,

00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:15.047
we don't have to defend any
particular set of values."

00:20:15.047 --> 00:20:17.115
When you say that,
then you just open

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:18.817 align:start size:84% position:16%
the door for the
Marxists to take over.

00:20:18.817 --> 00:20:23.822
The only way you can fight
a serious, public religion,

00:20:25.224 --> 00:20:27.559
or public philosophy, is with
another public philosophy.

00:20:30.495 --> 00:20:33.865 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So I get it, I get
you on the Liberal part.

00:20:33.865 --> 00:20:35.400
I talk about Bill
Maher all the time,

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.769
where the five remaining
sane Liberals in America,

00:20:37.769 --> 00:20:40.505 line:0%
they just are sort of in
this slow motion paralysis.

00:20:40.505 --> 00:20:42.274 line:0%
And two years later they get it.

00:20:42.274 --> 00:20:43.542 line:0%
They repeat what
a bunch of us say,

00:20:43.542 --> 00:20:44.843 line:0%
but they keep voting
for the wrong people.

00:20:44.843 --> 00:20:46.144 line:0%
So I'm with you on that.

00:20:46.144 --> 00:20:49.147
But what would you
say is not enough,

00:20:49.147 --> 00:20:51.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
for say what Ron DeSantis
is doing in Florida?

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:53.585 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I can telling you from
living her for four months,

00:20:53.585 --> 00:20:58.290 align:start position:0%
I'm living in a free state
that feels strong and defended.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:02.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is starkly
different than California,

00:21:02.928 --> 00:21:04.429
which made all of
the wrong decisions

00:21:04.429 --> 00:21:05.497
and went that route.

00:21:07.699 --> 00:21:09.735
- I think the number one thing

00:21:09.735 --> 00:21:14.740 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that sending kids
to schools where

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:18.877
five days a week,
or whatever it is,

00:21:20.012 --> 00:21:22.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
they spend their time
in an environment

00:21:22.781 --> 00:21:27.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is strict of
any reference to God,

00:21:27.152 --> 00:21:31.923 align:start size:97% position:3%
or to the Bible is the basis
of Western civilization.

00:21:31.923 --> 00:21:34.760
The Bible is the
fundamental text

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:37.663 align:start size:84% position:16%
on which Western
tradition was built.

00:21:38.997 --> 00:21:40.565
I think that that doesn't work.

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:46.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
I try to go into the
psychology of all of this,

00:21:47.372 --> 00:21:49.441
and how it actually works.

00:21:49.441 --> 00:21:52.177
'Cause I think people
don't understand this.

00:21:52.177 --> 00:21:56.882
If you want anything,
you know, young people

00:21:56.882 --> 00:21:58.717
are always saying, "What
do you mean Conservative?

00:21:58.717 --> 00:22:00.652
Conservatives don't
conserve anything."

00:22:00.652 --> 00:22:01.586
Right, you've heard that.

00:22:01.586 --> 00:22:03.055
People say that all the time.

00:22:04.256 --> 00:22:06.658
What have Conservatives
succeeded in conserving

00:22:06.658 --> 00:22:09.027
in the last 50 years?

00:22:09.027 --> 00:22:12.397
And I think we have to take
that argument seriously.

00:22:12.397 --> 00:22:15.801
There's a constant role
in cultural revolution.

00:22:15.801 --> 00:22:17.769
And the reason for
the constant role

00:22:17.769 --> 00:22:19.004
in cultural revolution,

00:22:19.004 --> 00:22:21.139
which just rips up one
thing after another,

00:22:21.139 --> 00:22:23.342
is because of the fact
that nobody's focused

00:22:24.276 --> 00:22:27.446
on how does the transmission,

00:22:27.446 --> 00:22:30.382
the conservation of
ideas, actually work?

00:22:30.382 --> 00:22:33.318 align:start size:81% position:19%
And for the way
it actually works,

00:22:33.318 --> 00:22:37.756 align:start size:97% position:3%
is that if you're a kid, and
you see that people give,

00:22:37.756 --> 00:22:40.559 align:start size:88% position:13%
the people around you
give honor to something,

00:22:41.526 --> 00:22:43.228
let's say the Bible.

00:22:43.228 --> 00:22:45.097
They give honor to
it. What do I mean?

00:22:45.097 --> 00:22:47.165
They say, "Look, this
is really important."

00:22:47.165 --> 00:22:50.268
Now, I'm not talking
about them saying,

00:22:50.268 --> 00:22:53.238
you have to believe this, or
if you don't believe this,

00:22:53.238 --> 00:22:55.073
then you're a terrible person.

00:22:55.073 --> 00:22:57.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm talking about
something much more basic.

00:22:57.776 --> 00:22:59.845 align:start size:88% position:13%
That if you're in an
environment where people

00:22:59.845 --> 00:23:03.215
are giving honor, they say,
"Look, this constitution is,

00:23:04.683 --> 00:23:08.520
the best that there's
been in the world.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:13.158 align:start size:88% position:13%
And this scripture is
the best moral framework

00:23:13.158 --> 00:23:15.761 align:start size:88% position:13%
for leading your life
that there's ever been."

00:23:15.761 --> 00:23:19.498 align:start size:88% position:13%
When you hear that from
people you respect,

00:23:19.498 --> 00:23:21.967
your mind opens up.

00:23:21.967 --> 00:23:24.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody's always saying,
"Oh, your mind closes."

00:23:24.069 --> 00:23:25.570
That's not my experience.

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:27.572
If people are saying, "Look,
this is just really important.

00:23:27.572 --> 00:23:29.474
You should take a look at it,"

00:23:29.474 --> 00:23:31.676
your mind opens up to learning.

00:23:33.145 --> 00:23:36.281
And right now, in America
and lots of other places,

00:23:36.281 --> 00:23:37.549
I mean this is true
for most of you,

00:23:37.549 --> 00:23:40.385
this is true for most
Democratic countries.

00:23:40.385 --> 00:23:43.422 align:start size:84% position:16%
The kids, the adults,
people's brains

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:46.291
are snapped shut like a trap.

00:23:46.291 --> 00:23:48.393 align:start size:84% position:16%
Somebody starts
talking about Bible,

00:23:48.393 --> 00:23:51.530
and they think, "Oh,
that's that primitive,

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:55.767 align:start size:84% position:16%
dark ages stuff
that we got rid of."

00:23:55.767 --> 00:23:58.303 align:start size:84% position:16%
People are scared
of it, people are...

00:23:59.771 --> 00:24:01.373 align:start size:81% position:19%
They just think
it's like you must

00:24:01.373 --> 00:24:04.176
be some kind of idiot for
talking about this stuff.

00:24:04.176 --> 00:24:09.181 align:start size:81% position:19%
And as long as the
Bible continues

00:24:10.248 --> 00:24:13.452 align:start size:88% position:13%
to be under this
shadow, instead of being

00:24:13.452 --> 00:24:16.087 align:start size:84% position:16%
this spectacular
document that created

