00:33:58.069 --> 00:34:00.705 align:start size:88% position:13%
was a more moderate
constitutional monarchy

00:34:00.705 --> 00:34:02.006
than what they had before.

00:34:03.274 --> 00:34:07.078 align:start size:84% position:16%
An example that's
closer to Americans,

00:34:07.078 --> 00:34:11.149 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the American
Constitution of 1787.

00:34:11.149 --> 00:34:12.683
You know, people think of,

00:34:12.683 --> 00:34:16.120 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I write about this at
some length in the new book,

00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:19.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
people think of the
American constitution,

00:34:19.590 --> 00:34:20.858
like they declared independence,

00:34:20.858 --> 00:34:21.893
and they wrote the constitution,

00:34:21.893 --> 00:34:23.194
there was like this miracle.

00:34:23.194 --> 00:34:25.396
And then they just got it right.

00:34:25.396 --> 00:34:26.798
But that's not what happened.

00:34:26.798 --> 00:34:28.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's almost the
opposite of what happened.

00:34:28.399 --> 00:34:31.736 align:start size:84% position:16%
What actually happened
is that in 1777,

00:34:33.871 --> 00:34:38.876 align:start size:97% position:3%
the Americans tried to step
away from the Anglo tradition.

00:34:39.744 --> 00:34:41.212
They wrote a constitution,

00:34:41.212 --> 00:34:42.980 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is called the Articles
of the Confederation,

00:34:42.980 --> 00:34:46.484
is what we call it today,
but it was a constitution.

00:34:46.484 --> 00:34:48.920
And George Washington
and his forces tried

00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:52.256 align:start size:97% position:3%
to fight a war against Britain
under that constitution.

00:34:52.256 --> 00:34:55.726
It was a weak constitution.
Its purpose was Liberty.

00:34:55.726 --> 00:34:58.329
Its purpose was to give as
much freedom as possible.

00:35:00.031 --> 00:35:03.301 align:start size:88% position:13%
It didn't give the
anybody enough strength

00:35:03.301 --> 00:35:08.306
to be able to do things like
raising an army, raising taxes,

00:35:10.541 --> 00:35:12.643
being able to impose

00:35:12.643 --> 00:35:14.178
a negotiated treaty
with another country

00:35:14.178 --> 00:35:18.583 align:start position:0%
being able to impose on the
states, the terms of the treaty.

00:35:18.583 --> 00:35:22.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after 11 years of this
chaos, I mean, where...

00:35:25.490 --> 00:35:28.726
The American army was
moved to Georgetown

00:35:28.726 --> 00:35:32.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
by people writing personal
checks as a donation,

00:35:32.497 --> 00:35:34.532
because the country was so weak.

00:35:35.733 --> 00:35:39.137
Washington came out
of this and he said,

00:35:39.137 --> 00:35:42.306
"We need something like
the English government,

00:35:42.306 --> 00:35:43.741
like the British government.

00:35:43.741 --> 00:35:46.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need some kind of
strong central government

00:35:46.144 --> 00:35:47.712
that protects freedom,

00:35:47.712 --> 00:35:51.883
but it has the ability to
raise an army, raise taxes,

00:35:54.285 --> 00:35:57.054
impose decisions
where necessary.

00:35:57.054 --> 00:35:59.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's how the American
constitution was born.

00:35:59.423 --> 00:36:03.194
It's a restoration of the
constitutional tradition

00:36:03.194 --> 00:36:06.164
of Anglo Americans.

00:36:06.164 --> 00:36:08.032
That restoration was
because they thought,

00:36:08.032 --> 00:36:09.367
we're going over the precipice.

00:36:09.367 --> 00:36:11.836
If you just think
for one second,

00:36:11.836 --> 00:36:15.573 align:start size:97% position:3%
like if they hadn't been
able to get private donations

00:36:15.573 --> 00:36:17.675
to get the army to Yorktown,

00:36:17.675 --> 00:36:19.777 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, they just could
have lost the war.

00:36:20.878 --> 00:36:22.280 align:start size:88% position:13%
