on my show for a
couple weeks now

00:36:23.781 --> 00:36:26.584 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we've begun to
enter a post-woke world.

00:36:26.584 --> 00:36:31.522 align:start size:88% position:13%
I do see a fight against
the woke movement,

00:36:31.522 --> 00:36:33.558 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Marxism that
you're talking about.

00:36:33.558 --> 00:36:35.993 align:start size:88% position:13%
And you're talking
about checks being sent

00:36:35.993 --> 00:36:37.361
to keep the army going.

00:36:37.361 --> 00:36:40.965
And, you know, Elon
Musk buying Twitter,

00:36:40.965 --> 00:36:44.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
one federal judge
reversing the mask mandate,

00:36:44.001 --> 00:36:46.904 align:start size:88% position:13%
individual people trying
for that restoration

00:36:46.904 --> 00:36:48.039 align:start size:81% position:19%
is an interesting-
- Right.

00:36:48.039 --> 00:36:50.107 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Is the most
American thing perhaps

00:36:50.107 --> 00:36:51.475
that you could possibly do.

00:36:51.475 --> 00:36:54.378 align:start position:0%
So let's link this to
something a little more recent.

00:36:54.378 --> 00:36:56.714 align:start size:88% position:13%
So at the National
Conservatism Conference,

00:36:56.714 --> 00:37:01.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
which was at the
end of October 2021,

00:37:01.385 --> 00:37:03.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
you me, Sohrab Ahmar,
who I mentioned earlier,

00:37:03.888 --> 00:37:06.290
and Douglas Murray were all on
a panel where we were trying

00:37:06.290 --> 00:37:09.060
to do just what we've
been discussing here.

00:37:09.060 --> 00:37:10.661
That we were trying
to piece together,

00:37:10.661 --> 00:37:12.496
how do you take the
traditional sort

00:37:12.496 --> 00:37:15.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
of religious
conservative perspective?

00:37:15.366 --> 00:37:16.767
Where do you blend that with

00:37:16.767 --> 00:37:18.269 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Classical
Liberal perspective?

00:37:18.269 --> 00:37:21.672 align:start size:88% position:13%
How do you take a purely
secular Libertarian,

00:37:21.672 --> 00:37:25.643
and the more, even the more
traditional Conservative?

00:37:25.643 --> 00:37:29.013
how do you take all of this,
combine all of these people

00:37:29.013 --> 00:37:30.214
with all of their difference,

00:37:30.214 --> 00:37:32.049 align:start size:84% position:16%
make it into something
that's whole?

00:37:32.049 --> 00:37:33.551 align:start size:88% position:13%
And what was
particularly interesting

00:37:33.551 --> 00:37:35.019
about the conversation,

00:37:35.019 --> 00:37:37.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
which we'll link to below,
so people can see it,

00:37:37.855 --> 00:37:39.924
is that two of the
four panelists up

00:37:39.924 --> 00:37:41.225
there happened to be gay.

00:37:41.225 --> 00:37:43.794 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now that obviously,
is a minority

00:37:43.794 --> 00:37:46.831 align:start size:88% position:13%
from a sexuality
perspective, let's say.

00:37:46.831 --> 00:37:48.833 align:start size:81% position:19%
And we were really
trying to hash

00:37:48.833 --> 00:37:51.369 align:start size:97% position:3%
through these issues in about
an hour and a half talk,

00:37:51.369 --> 00:37:53.137 align:start size:81% position:19%
and nothing was
left on the table,

00:37:53.137 --> 00:37:54.939 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we took questions
from everybody.

00:37:54.939 --> 00:37:57.108
Where do you see that now?

00:37:57.108 --> 00:37:58.909
And I don't know that,
I don't think we all got

00:37:58.909 --> 00:38:01.412 align:start size:84% position:16%
to a full conclusion
on it, exactly.

00:38:01.412 --> 00:38:03.247
I think Sohrab and
Douglas definitely

00:38:03.247 --> 00:38:05.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
had some big
disagreements by the end.

00:38:05.049 --> 00:38:06.384
But where do you fall on that?

00:38:06.384 --> 00:38:10.488
- Look, I'm glad that
we did the experiment

00:38:10.488 --> 00:38:13.591
And not only that, but
I'd like to keep trying

00:38:13.591 --> 00:38:14.859
to do the experiment because I-

00:38:14.859 --> 00:38:15.793
- Yeah.

00:38:15.793 --> 00:38:17.762
- Because I think the reality is

00:38:19.263 --> 00:38:24.268 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there's all these Liberal
refugees who are, you know,

00:38:25.136 --> 00:38:26.370
they're moving to the right,

00:38:26.370 --> 00:38:28.072
because they can see
something terrible

00:38:28.072 --> 00:38:29.740
is happening on the left.

00:38:33.377 --> 00:38:34.845
And Elon Musk. I don't
know if you saw him,

00:38:34.845 --> 00:38:37.281
he tweeted this image.

00:38:37.281 --> 00:38:39.383 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh, I saw it, we
played it on the show.

00:38:39.383 --> 00:38:43.287
- Right. So I think a lot
of people feel like that.

00:38:43.287 --> 00:38:46.223
He says, "Look, I've never
been anything but a Liberal,

00:38:46.223 --> 00:38:47.725 align:start size:84% position:16%
but now I'm clearly
on the Right.

00:38:47.725 --> 00:38:50.027
It's not that I've moved,
but the spectrum has moved.

00:38:50.027 --> 00:38:53.597 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's being pulled like taffy
by the revolutionaries."

00:38:53.597 --> 00:38:57.234
And so he sees himself now
as being part of the Right.

00:39:01.138 --> 00:39:03.007 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's what's happening,
and what that means

00:39:03.007 --> 00:39:05.209
is we have no choice.

00:39:05.209 --> 00:39:08.312
There's going to have to
be some kind of alliance

00:39:08.312 --> 00:39:10.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
between Conservative
and Liberals.

00:39:10.848 --> 00:39:13.617 align:start size:88% position:13%
But that doesn't mean
that this is easy to do.

00:39:17.321 --> 00:39:20.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't think that particular
thing worked out so well.

00:39:20.991 --> 00:39:22.426
Douglas came out of it,

00:39:23.894 --> 00:39:27.164
and he felt like he needed
to write an essay saying,

00:39:28.599 --> 00:39:32.703
"These conservatives, they're
too much, they're too far."

00:39:33.804 --> 00:39:35.539 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't know if you saw that.
- Yeah.

00:39:35.539 --> 00:39:37.408
- Like two weeks after he-

00:39:37.408 --> 00:39:39.043
- I've had Douglas on
my show since then,

00:39:39.043 --> 00:39:40.344
and we discussed, yeah.

00:39:40.344 --> 00:39:42.680
- Okay. So that was him.

00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:45.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Sohrab responded
to him by saying,

00:39:45.616 --> 00:39:47.852
"I just don't see
how this can work."

00:39:47.852 --> 00:39:52.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
And look, I'm not
terribly surprised, but...

00:39:55.259 --> 00:39:58.362
- But that tension that
you're talking about,

00:39:58.362 --> 00:39:59.830
I get it exists.

00:39:59.830 --> 00:40:01.832 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's why, I mean,
for years I've been saying,

00:40:01.832 --> 00:40:04.301
if there is some sort of
new Conservative movement

00:40:04.301 --> 00:40:06.670 align:start size:84% position:16%
on the horizon, I
still no matter what

00:40:06.670 --> 00:40:08.773
at the end of the day,
will probably end up

00:40:08.773 --> 00:40:10.975 align:start size:88% position:13%
on the more
Libertarian side of it,

00:40:10.975 --> 00:40:12.810 align:start size:84% position:16%
or classically
Liberal side of it.

00:40:12.810 --> 00:40:16.147 line:0%
I think we're all trying to
do something that's tough.

00:40:16.147 --> 00:40:18.048 line:0%
And when you try to do
something that's tough,

00:40:18.048 --> 00:40:19.283 line:0%
or as Jordan Peterson would say,

00:40:19.283 --> 00:40:21.185 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
when we were on
tour all the time,

00:40:21.185 --> 00:40:23.521 align:start size:88% position:13%
that healthy tension
that perhaps we all want

00:40:23.521 --> 00:40:26.023
between Liberalism
and Conservatism,

00:40:26.023 --> 00:40:28.526
it's hard to balance
that all the time.

00:40:28.526 --> 00:40:32.096
And maybe it can't, maybe
it just can't be done.

00:40:32.096 --> 00:40:33.697
Maybe it can't be done
at a national level.

00:40:33.697 --> 00:40:37.468
I think perhaps it could be
done at a personal level.

00:40:37.468 --> 00:40:42.339
- I think you're a model
in what you just said.

00:40:42.339 --> 00:40:45.342
That people can disagree,
and in the end of the day,

00:40:45.342 --> 00:40:48.045
we ought to be able to just
go have scotch together.

00:40:48.045 --> 00:40:52.683
And I do everything I can
to live like that myself.

00:40:54.118 --> 00:40:57.521
In that, I'm following
the way that you talk

00:40:57.521 --> 00:40:59.490
to people in the studio.

00:40:59.490 --> 00:41:03.294
I really think that this,
that discussion should be

00:41:05.162 --> 00:41:08.265 align:start size:84% position:16%
amicable between
people who are like...

00:41:08.265 --> 00:41:09.733
We're not enemies,

00:41:09.733 --> 00:41:12.536
we're friends who have
important disagreements.

00:41:12.536 --> 00:41:15.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
- And by the way, removing
me from the equation.

00:41:15.406 --> 00:41:17.208 align:start size:88% position:13%
If there's a
Conservative out there,

00:41:17.208 --> 00:41:19.343 align:start size:88% position:13%
a religious
Conservative who thinks

00:41:19.343 --> 00:41:21.011
that Douglas Murray is not

00:41:21.011 --> 00:41:23.080 align:start size:84% position:16%
a good enough
Conservative for them,

00:41:23.080 --> 00:41:26.083
then that's not my brand of
Conservatism, how about that?

00:41:26.083 --> 00:41:27.485
- Well, no-

00:41:27.485 --> 00:41:29.119 align:start position:0%
- To remove us from the
equation for a moment, you know?

00:41:29.119 --> 00:41:31.255
- Well, Douglas is, look.

00:41:32.356 --> 00:41:33.924 align:start size:84% position:16%
Douglas is a little
bit different,

00:41:33.924 --> 00:41:38.062 align:start size:97% position:3%
because Douglas doesn't
claim to be a Conservative.

00:41:38.062 --> 00:41:39.930
He doesn't claim to
be a Nationalist.

00:41:41.332 --> 00:41:45.870
He comes to the conferences
and he says things like,

00:41:45.870 --> 00:41:48.439 align:start size:97% position:3%
"You know, I probably agree
with 1/3 of the things

00:41:48.439 --> 00:41:50.074
that are being stated here."

00:41:50.074 --> 00:41:54.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
He deflates, you
know, he participates,
he's a great friend.

00:41:55.312 --> 00:41:56.881
He participates fully,

00:41:56.881 --> 00:41:59.149
but he doesn't,

00:42:01.118 --> 00:42:05.456 align:start size:97% position:3%
he doesn't take a leadership
role among Conservatives

00:42:05.456 --> 00:42:06.824
the way that you do.

00:42:06.824 --> 00:42:08.292 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I'm not blaming
you for this.

00:42:08.292 --> 00:42:09.593
I mean, I think everybody,

00:42:10.794 --> 00:42:12.796
everybody has just
been really happy

00:42:12.796 --> 00:42:14.999
to have somebody like
you taking leadership.

00:42:18.669 --> 00:42:21.272
I think it's hit a bump
and I don't, you know,

00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:24.875 align:start size:88% position:13%
I regret that, I'm
really sorry about that,

00:42:24.875 --> 00:42:26.810 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I'm looking
forward to the scotch.

00:42:26.810 --> 00:42:29.580
- (laughs) Listen, I
probably can't solve

00:42:29.580 --> 00:42:33.017 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of the existential
issues for all of the people

00:42:33.017 --> 00:42:36.353 align:start size:97% position:3%
that come at this from a
purely religious perspective.

00:42:36.353 --> 00:42:40.491 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think it's a great
challenge to blend a society

00:42:40.491 --> 00:42:43.427
from a traditional and
religious perspective

00:42:43.427 --> 00:42:46.430
that also has an awful lot
of secular people in it.

00:42:46.430 --> 00:42:48.299
Although you happen to be
in the swamp right now,

00:42:48.299 --> 00:42:51.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
you live in a country that's
only 70 plus years old

00:42:51.902 --> 00:42:53.871
that has done a pretty good job,

00:42:53.871 --> 00:42:56.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
but often an imperfect
job of blending

00:42:56.807 --> 00:42:59.143
the secular and the traditional.

00:42:59.143 --> 00:43:00.678 align:start size:81% position:19%
I suppose the best
thing we can do

00:43:00.678 --> 00:43:02.880
is continue to have
these conversations.

00:43:02.880 --> 00:43:03.714
- Right.

00:43:05.015 --> 00:43:09.486 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yoram, the book is
"Conservatism: A Rediscovery."

00:43:09.486 --> 00:43:11.088
And we will do that whiskey

00:43:11.088 --> 00:43:12.856
and/or tequila soon, my friend.

00:43:12.856 --> 00:43:14.058 align:start size:75% position:25%
Good seeing you.
(book thuds)

00:43:14.058 --> 00:43:16.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay. Thank you,
Dave, good to see you.

